[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,10.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(12.5,0);
\foreach \y in {3,6,9,12,15} {\draw (-0.2,\y/1.5)--(0,\y/1.5); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y/1.5) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.8,0) rectangle (2.8,2.67);
\draw (2.8,0) rectangle (4.8,6.0);
\draw (4.8,0) rectangle (6.8,10.0);
\draw (6.8,0) rectangle (8.8,5.33);
\draw (8.8,0) rectangle (10.8,2.67);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {1.8/10, 3.8/20, 5.8/30, 7.8/40, 9.8/50} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,5) {Frequency};
\node[below] at (5.8,-1.0) {Class centre};
\node at (5.8,11.0) {Student test marks};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The frequency histogram shows the scores of $40$ students with class centres $10, 20, 30, 40, 50$ and frequencies $4, 9, 15, 8, 4$.
How many students scored in a class with class centre $30$ or higher?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,10.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(10.5,0);
\foreach \y in {20,40,60,80} {\draw (-0.2,\y/10)--(0,\y/10); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y/10) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.8,0) rectangle (2.8,1.2);
\draw (2.8,0) rectangle (4.8,3.4);
\draw (4.8,0) rectangle (6.8,7.0);
\draw (6.8,0) rectangle (8.8,8.0);
\draw[thick] (0.8,0)--(2.8,1.2)--(4.8,3.4)--(6.8,7.0)--(8.8,8.0);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0.8/0, 2.8/20, 4.8/40, 6.8/60, 8.8/80} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,4.5) {Cumulative frequency};
\node[below] at (4.8,-1.0) {Age (years)};
\node at (4.8,10.0) {Ages of club members};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The cumulative frequency histogram and ogive show the ages of $80$ club members, with upper class boundaries $20, 40, 60, 80$ and cumulative frequencies $12, 34, 70, 80$.
How many members are in the age group $40$ to $60$ years?
